{
  "_help": [
    "Maps the pretrained Discogs styles to DJ genre names. No training needed.",
    "Each genre lists one or more 'needs' groups. A genre scores as high as its WEAKEST group",
    "(each group scores as its strongest Discogs style), so 'Acid Trance' needs both an acid",
    "style AND a trance style. Genres with 2+ groups get a small bonus for being more specific, but only",
    "when different styles fill the groups (Acid House alone in both groups of 'Acid House' gets none).",
    "'bpm' is the usual tempo range; tracks outside it are scored lower (gradually, down to 60% at 3 BPM outside), not excluded. Leave 'bpm' out for music with no steady beat (Ambient): tempo then plays no part.",
    "Edit freely. To keep your edits safe from updates, copy this file to data/dj_genres.json.",
    "Style names must match Discogs exactly; run `uv run server.py styles` to list them all.",
    "Neo Trance, Hard Beat, Doomcore and J-Core only exist in the MAEST model (519 styles).",
    "Neo Trance sits in Melodic House & Techno, not Trance: MAEST gives it to modern melodic house at 120-128 (tested 2026-11-11: 27 tracks with Neo Trance on top, shop tags melodic house/techno, none trance).",
    "Electro House is left inside House on purpose: the models give Discogs' 2010s 'Electro House' to most modern melodic/peak-time house (tested 2026-10-22: 49 of 82 House tracks).",
    "Avoid '/' and ';' in genre names: Navidrome splits genres on them, and ';' separates multiple genres."
  ],
